<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zolta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Zoltán, Grand Prince of the Hungarians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zolta, or Zoltán, was a Hungarian grand prince of the 10th century, the youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a> he married the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menumorut">Menumorut</a> and inherited his lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>. Hungarian chronicles name him as Árpád's successor, but the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a> does not mention him, and his reign and dates are uncertain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zolta.jpg" alt="Zolta" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sculptor: ? photo: own work · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solt_in_Solt.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
